{
  "id": "P005",
  "slug": "caesar-cipher",
  "title": "Caesar Cipher Tag Encoder",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": [
    "strings"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 12,
  "relatedModules": [
    "a3-strings-io",
    "a5-functions"
  ],
  "entry": {
    "type": "function",
    "name": "caesar_shift"
  },
  "compare": "exact",
  "tests": {
    "visible": [
      {
        "label": "Positive shift wrapping z to b",
        "args": [
          "Alert-Z9",
          3
        ],
        "expected": "Dohuw-C9"
      },
      {
        "label": "Negative decode shift",
        "args": [
          "Dohuw-C9",
          -3
        ],
        "expected": "Alert-Z9"
      }
    ],
    "hidden": [
      {
        "label": "Zero shift preserves exact string",
        "args": [
          "Ticket_42!",
          0
        ],
        "expected": "Ticket_42!"
      },
      {
        "label": "Large shift greater than 26",
        "args": [
          "abcXYZ",
          29
        ],
        "expected": "defABC"
      },
      {
        "label": "Large negative shift",
        "args": [
          "abcXYZ",
          -29
        ],
        "expected": "xyzUVW"
      },
      {
        "label": "Full alphabet round-trip shift 26",
        "args": [
          "DataPath",
          26
        ],
        "expected": "DataPath"
      },
      {
        "label": "Empty text",
        "args": [
          "",
          13
        ],
        "expected": ""
      }
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "Lowercase and uppercase letters form two separate 26-letter rings; digits, spaces, and symbols stay unchanged.",
    "Compute base = ord(\"a\") if ch.islower() else ord(\"A\"), normalize k = shift % 26, and map chr(base + (ord(ch) - base + k) % 26).",
    "Pseudocode:\n  k = shift % 26\n  for ch in text:\n      if \"a\" <= ch <= \"z\": shift relative to ord(\"a\")\n      elif \"A\" <= ch <= \"Z\": shift relative to ord(\"A\")\n      else: keep ch unchanged"
  ],
  "sources": [
    "python-tutorial",
    "python-stdtypes-docs"
  ]
}
